  "description": "KAKBIK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C33 H33 F42 O10 Sm3,C33 H31 F42 O10 Sm3. From the CIF bond table, Sm1A (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm2A (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm3A (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm2B (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm1B (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm3B (Sm) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.725-3.803 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.05-101.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C33H32F42O10Sm3.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
